# This repo has three separate Node projects (cli/, web/, action/) alongside
# the Python backend. Only requirements.txt and app/ are ever COPYed into
# the backend image, but without this file Docker still tars up and sends
# the *entire* build context (repo root) to the daemon before evaluating
# any COPY instruction -- so excluding their node_modules/build output here
# is what actually keeps `docker build` fast, not the Dockerfile's COPY list.

.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.local
*.md

**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

web/.next/
web/data/
web/.env.local

action/test/

sample_logs/
scripts/
